#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# difference_root

#% text
# `difference_root(f)` stands for the sequence defined by `f(y, n)`: a list of a linear recurrence for y(n) and enough initial values. `difference_root(f)(k)` gives its k-th term.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Terms at integers are computed by running the recurrence forward with `recurrence_table`; a list of integers gives a list of terms. Symbolic parameters stay in the terms, which are expanded. At an inexact number with an integer value the term is given as a number.

#% item
# Written form: equal definitions are written alike. The formal names are `FormalY` and `FormalN`; the recurrence is P == 0, where P is the numerator of lhs - rhs over a common denominator, collected in the terms y(n + j) with expanded coefficients, its content free of n divided out and the coefficient of the highest shift with a positive first number; the terms free of y come first, then y(n + j) by increasing shift; the initial values follow by their point.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
difference_root((y, k) => [y(k + 2) == y(k + 1) + y(k), y(0) == 0, y(1) == 1])(20)
#% output
#= 6765

#% cell
difference_root((y, k) => [y(k + 1) == (k + 1)*y(k), y(1) == 1])([3, 5, 10])
#% output
#= [6, 120, 3628800]

#% cell
difference_root((y, k) => [y(k + 2) == x*y(k + 1) - (k + 1)*y(k), y(0) == 1, y(1) == 1])(4)
#% output
#= 3 - 5*x - x^2 + x^3

#% cell
difference_root((y, n) => [y(n + 2) == y(n + 1) - y(n)/2, y(0) == 0, y(1) == 1])
#% output
#= difference_root((FormalY, FormalN) => [FormalY(FormalN) - 2*FormalY(1 + FormalN) + 2*FormalY(2 + FormalN) == 0, FormalY(0) == 0, FormalY(1) == 1])

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `differential_root`, `recurrence_table`, `r_solve`
